{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 40,
  "title": "Describing people",
  "description": "Say what a person is like, and make the adjective match.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "These adjectives describe what somebody is like, not how they are at the moment. They go after ser, and they change their ending for the person they describe.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The adjectives",
        "body": "Alto, gordo, delgado, guapo, simpático, inteligente, divertido, serio, bonito and feo. The feminine is the same word with -a instead of -o: el simpático is un hombre simpático, la simpática is una mujer simpática. Guapo and feo change in the same way.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "es alto",
            "en": "he is tall"
          },
          {
            "es": "es simpática",
            "en": "she is friendly"
          },
          {
            "es": "es un inteligente",
            "en": "he is an intelligent person"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "With ser, not estar",
        "body": "What somebody is like is ser: es alto, es simpático. What somebody is like at this moment is estar: está alto, está cansado. A person is usually described with ser, because being tall or being friendly is part of what they are.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "mi hermana es guapa",
            "en": "my sister is beautiful"
          },
          {
            "es": "mi hermana está guapa hoy",
            "en": "my sister looks beautiful today"
          },
          {
            "es": "el médico es serio",
            "en": "the doctor is serious"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
